                                "text": "lipped pitcher"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f9d87ff1-8e3d-3850-8f2c-9eecde7c478c",
                        "entry_id": "8c27d8e3-8f84-3bfd-92d2-168e666d8eaa",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Having some specific type of lip."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "in-compounds",
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "621e5ff2-9005-46ec-ad71-92dd8a8c55dd",
                                "sense_id": "f9d87ff1-8e3d-3850-8f2c-9eecde7c478c",
                                "text": "[…] it seemes a holy quire\nFounded to th’ name of great Apollo’s lyre,\nWhose silver-roofe rings with the sprightly notes\nOf sweet-lipp’d angel-imps, that swill their throats\nIn creame of morning Helicon […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "88248377-0104-47eb-8a8a-1380dfb547a0",
                                "sense_id": "f9d87ff1-8e3d-3850-8f2c-9eecde7c478c",
                                "text": "1814, William Wordsworth, The Excursion, London: Longman, Hurst, Rees, Orme & Brown, Book Four, p. 191,\n[…] I have seen\nA curious Child, who dwelt upon a tract\nOf inland ground, applying to his ear\nThe convolutions of a smooth-lipped Shell;"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2dd5630a-37e3-4da9-89d6-294318ce3010",
                                "sense_id": "f9d87ff1-8e3d-3850-8f2c-9eecde7c478c",
                                "text": "And all the while the thick-lipped leviathan is rushing through the deep, leaving tons of tumultuous white curds in his wake […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7e883914-71d1-4d99-8d5a-564d509eca63",
                                "sense_id": "f9d87ff1-8e3d-3850-8f2c-9eecde7c478c",
                                "text": "Amory squeezed into the back seat beside a gaudy, vermilion-lipped blonde."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8d7643aa-cb4b-4a38-a5ab-66048fda8b0b",
                                "sense_id": "f9d87ff1-8e3d-3850-8f2c-9eecde7c478c",
                                "text": "1933, George R. Preedy (Marjorie Bowen), Double Dallilay (U.S. title Queen’s Caprice), Part 1,\nThe two French girls held the gilt-lipped vases of milk and slowly poured them into the alabaster bath."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c2cb1e31-2d15-45cc-8354-60cf01100e8c",
                                "sense_id": "f9d87ff1-8e3d-3850-8f2c-9eecde7c478c",
                                "text": "[He] furrowed his brow, opened his eyes wider and wider until they were expressionless, and attempted to set his small, plump-lipped mouth."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cb20b8a0-c0e2-4435-be01-8525fc6869f3",
                                "sense_id": "f9d87ff1-8e3d-3850-8f2c-9eecde7c478c",
                                "text": "We met a yellow-lipped woman."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
